::: {.doc-subject}

Check if the graph itself is a triad: a directed graph with three nodes and no self-loops.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L40985-L41042){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}
```pythonsignature
Graph.is_triad()
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

![Is triad](../assets/graphs/is-triad.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt="Left: a directed graph on three nodes A, B, C with the single arc A to B and no self-loops, so is_triad() returns True. Right: three nodes in an undirected graph (named in the accent note above it); a triad must be directed, so is_triad() returns False." width="100%"}
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   `True` for a directed graph with exactly three nodes and no self-loops.
:::

## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}

Matches NetworkX's `is_triad`.

## See Also {.doc-see-also}

[](`~triad_type`) 

:   Classify the triad formed by three nodes.

[](`~all_triads`) 

:   List every triad of a directed graph.

## Examples {.doc-examples}

A triad has three nodes and no self-loops, whatever its arcs:

::: {#d127a8c3 .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import edgecase as ec

three = ec.Graph.from_edges([("A", "B")], directed=True).add_node("C")

three.is_triad(), ec.Graph().add_nodes(["A", "B", "C"]).is_triad()
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}
```
(True, False)
```
:::
:::


### Taking one triad out

`payments()` is a month of payments between 18 accounts at a made-up bank, each directed
from payer to payee. The subgraph of Ana, Ben and Cruz is a triad, holding just the
three payments of their ring:

::: {#e27e8875 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
payments = ec.payments()
ring = payments.subgraph(
    [payments.get_id_from_label(name) for name in ["Ana", "Ben", "Cruz"]]
)

ring.is_triad(), ring.triad_type(ring.get_node_ids())
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```
(True, '030C')
```
:::
:::


::: {#adb5a013 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
ring.plot(
    label_by="label", edge_label_by="amount", width=320, height=300
)
```

